```--------------------Here is the required C# code:

```cs
Debug.Assert(File.Exists(fileName));
```
In the provided code snippet, the Debug.Assert statement is used to check if the file exists. If the file does not exist, an AssertionFailure exception will be thrown. This is helpful in identifying issues during testing and debugging.--------------------```cs
void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
	bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);
	// csharp code that uses "Debug.Assert"
	Debug.Assert(templatesFileExist);
}

```--------------------```cs
// The template file exists
Debug.Assert(templatesFileExist);
```
Please note that the Debug.Assert is a tool to debug your code in Visual Studio. It checks a condition and if it does not meet the expected result, it sends an AssertionFailedException. This can be helpful when you are testing your code and want to make sure that a certain condition is true.--------------------```cs
void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
    bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);
    // @@@ Assert.IsTrue(templatesFileExist);
}

```
